cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DH-Tracker-2026 in published work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "DH-Tracker-2026: 3D tracking of fluorescent beads imaged through a double-helix point spread function"
abstract: >-
  DH-Tracker-2026 finds fluorescent beads imaged through a double-helix point spread function (DH-PSF),
  measures their 3D position in every frame from the rotation of the two lobes using a calibration z-scan,
  links them into tracks, analyses how each bead moves, and maps the deformation of the material, with an
  interactive browser app for inspecting the results and starting new analyses.
authors:
  - family-names: Weiss
    given-names: Lucien E.
    email: lucien.weiss@polymtl.ca
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0971-7329"
    affiliation: "Department of Engineering Physics and Lassonde DeepTech Institute, Polytechnique Montréal, Montréal H3T 1J4, Québec, Canada"
repository-code: "https://github.com/WeissLab/DH-Tracker"
url: "https://www.weisslab.ca"
license: BSD-3-Clause
date-released: "2026-09-28"
keywords:
  - double-helix point spread function
  - single-particle tracking
  - 3D localization microscopy
  - fluorescent beads
  - indentation
  - deformation mapping
